Step 2.2: Implement the save_new_agent_definition Action

This is the key to making your system "learn." It's a powerful admin-level action that creates a new, versioned agent definition.

    Action: Create a new local action in Go.

    Pseudo-code (Go):
    Go

    // in a new file, e.g., platform/orchestration/actions/admin_actions.go
    func SaveNewAgentDefinitionAction(ctx context.Context, params ActionParams) (interface{}, error) {
        // 1. Get the approved prompt from `params.CollectedData["human_feedback"]`.
        // 2. Get the original agent type (e.g., "html-developer") from the initial request data.
        // 3. Determine the next version number (e.g., if "html-developer" exists, this becomes "html-developer-v2").
        // 4. Read the full definition of the original agent from the `agent_definitions` table.
        // 5. Create a new definition object, copying all fields but updating:
        //    - The `type` name to the new versioned name.
        //    - The `prompt_template` to the new, human-approved prompt.
        // 6. INSERT this new object as a new row into the `agent_definitions` table.
        // 7. Return the new agent type name (e.g., "html-developer-v2").
    }

